  "schema": "vigil-whatwg-encoding-conformance/1",
  "note": "Conformance corpus for the WHATWG 'get an encoding' step (integration/vigil_integration/live/body_decode.py:_whatwg_codec) and the security-relevant decode remaps. A browser resolves a Content-Type charset LABEL through the WHATWG Encoding Standard's FIXED label table — NOT a regex and NOT Python's codec registry (which accepts labels a browser rejects and remaps others differently). This corpus is an INDEPENDENT restatement of the spec (authored from https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/, not derived from the implementation), checked against the code by integration/tests/test_whatwg_encoding_conformance.py. 'status' is the value _whatwg_codec returns: 'ok' (a byte-faithful codec VIGIL decodes), 'unsupported' (a WHATWG-recognized label VIGIL cannot decode faithfully offline — refused, INCONCLUSIVE), 'unknown' (not a WHATWG label at all — a browser ignores the header). Both non-ok statuses resolve to body-unavailable, so a body-dependent negative over them is INCONCLUSIVE, never CLEAN.",
  "source": "WHATWG Encoding Standard — Encodings table + the decode remaps that matter for markup adjudication.",
